# The planning map's grab: a press takes hold of the mission row whose GMapMarkerRect the pointer
# last came onto, CurentRectMarker - the 50 by 50 rect addpolygonmarker puts round each marker,
# 25 either side of the point and from 45 above it to 5 below, so the pin standing on the point
# is in it (ExtLibs/Maps/GMapMarkerRect.cs:43-52; GCSViews/FlightPlanner.cs:7378-7487, 8065-8134).
# A drag from there moves the row; a click there adds nothing - "cant add WP in existing rect"
# (FlightPlanner.cs:7733-7742) - where the port's old 14-pixel circle about the point missed the
# pin's head and added a waypoint on top of it.
#
# The map's pixels are not the script's: 0.04 of its height is some 30 pixels on a 1600 by 1200
# window, above the point and well inside the rect.

env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
screen plan
window 1600x1200
budget 10
# A first budget, set by hand until a passing run records one.

# The map first: a press before its first paint records nothing.
expect map.ready true
click map@0.45x0.40
click map@0.60x0.55
expect mission.items 2

# A click on waypoint 2's pin, above its point: its rect, the row selected and nothing added.
click map@0.60x0.52
expect map.rect 2
expect mission.items 2
expect mission.selected 2

# A drag from waypoint 1's pin head moves it: no waypoint added where the press was or where it
# was let go, and the pointer then on its marker at the new place. The pointer leaves waypoint 2's
# rect first: GMap enters and leaves the rects of one move in the overlay's order, so a jump
# straight from 2's into 1's would enter 1's and then, leaving 2's, leave none current.
hover map@0.10x0.10
expect map.rect none
drag map@0.45x0.36 map@0.30x0.62
expect mission.items 2
expect mission.selected 1
hover map@0.30x0.61
expect map.hover 1

# Below a point by more than 5 pixels is off its rect: a click there adds a waypoint.
click map@0.60x0.58
expect mission.items 3
